     iiffssttaatteedd — Interface State daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     iiffssttaatteedd [--ddhhiinnvv] [--DD _m_a_c_r_o=_v_a_l_u_e] [--ff _f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiffssttaatteedd daemon runs commands in response to network state changes,
     which it determines by monitoring interface link state or running exter‐
     nal tests.  For example, it can be used with carp(4) to change running
     services or to ensure that carp(4) interfaces stay in sync, or with pf(4)
     to test server or link availability and modify translation or routing
     rules.  The options are as follows:

     --DD _m_a_c_r_o=_v_a_l_u_e
             Define _m_a_c_r_o to be set to _v_a_l_u_e on the command line.  Overrides
             the definition of _m_a_c_r_o in the configuration file.

     --dd      Do not daemonize and log to _s_t_d_o_u_t.

     --ff _f_i_l_e
             Specify an alternate location, _f_i_l_e, for the configuration file.

     --hh      Print help message.

     --ii      Ignore initial interface states.

     --nn      Configtest mode.  Check config validity, then exit.

     --vv      Verbose mode.  Use twice to further increase verbosity.

     Upon receiving SIGHUP, iiffssttaatteedd reloads the configuration file.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/ifstated.conf  iiffssttaatteedd configuration file.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     carp(4), pf(4), ifstated.conf(5)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
